		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5876C6E6DB7E0074"]
			description: ["The plain wall of the horizon age: a bound degenerate billet braced by tensegrity trusses. Every large structure of the age, from the press to the array, is mostly this. An assembler, 200 ticks: a bound degenerate billet, two Kerr strand wires, two tensegrity truss casings, a MAX sensor,     two FFKM seals and a quarter bucket of superfluid helium-3, for four casings. Every horizon structure, and the Kerr coil casing. Billets and wire by ME; the helium-3 by pipe. Make it by the thousand: one structure takes thousands of blocks."]
			icon: "grindless:bound_lattice_casing"
			id: "5175DDABD9A78869"
			rewards: [{ id: "5C424AFB8F22C1F6", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
