			title: "Iris Blade"
			x: 36.0d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F699D8ACB0E6834"]
			description: ["Step 1 of the helium-3 polarisation line: primordial deuterium and hydrogen are made to meet on platinum, so half of the molecules become HD. A chemical reactor, 400 ticks: one platinum dust, primordial deuterium and hydrogen in equal parts, for twice that of HD equilibrium mix. Pure HD. Hydrogen and deuterium by pipe; platinum by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:hd_equilibrium_mix_bucket"
			id: "33F21654A7D76A69"
			rewards: [{ id: "3B6C123F4B217CC7", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "3906FD184F5A5440", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "HD Equilibrium Mix"
			x: 23.5d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["33F21654A7D76A69"]
			description: ["Step 2: the mix is distilled. The plain hydrogen and deuterium that come out go back into the reactor. A distillation tower, 400 ticks: the mix gives pure HD, and half as much again returns as hydrogen and primordial deuterium in equal parts. Frozen-spin HD. Pipe the two returned fluids back to step 1: the loop is closed."]
			icon: "gtceu:pure_hd_bucket"
			id: "3B0D3ED6742D947D"
			rewards: [{ id: "1AAA3D1422B399D4", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "73F26BF9D6687CD2", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Pure HD"
			x: 26.0d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B0D3ED6742D947D"]
			description: ["Step 3: HD cooled to a few millikelvin in a field keeps its spins in line. It is the spin-ordered target of the horizon fusion lines. The nuclear demagnetisation cooler, 2,400 ticks: pure HD, for one frozen-spin HD. Spin-ordered targets for the horizon fusion lines. Pure HD by pipe; the target out by bus."]
			icon: "grindless:frozen_spin_hd"
			id: "514C730C492510AA"
			rewards: [{ id: "18F91ADDDB53A5C8", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "544A9648BD20EEFF", item: "grindless:frozen_spin_hd", type: "item" }]
			title: "Frozen-Spin HD"
			x: 28.5d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["514C730C492510AA"]
			description: ["Step 4: pristine helium-3 is pumped with a MAX emitter so that its spins line up. It feeds the polarised fusion stellarator. The photonic foundry, 1,200 ticks: pristine helium-3 and a MAX emitter, which is only rarely used up. Polarised fusion. Pristine helium-3 by pipe from its line; replace emitters from ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:polarized_helium_3_bucket"
			id: "3F2040A000B7B950"
			rewards: [{ id: "54E502645D8CC574", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "76FA6A88C2DD6F7B", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Polarised Helium-3"
			x: 31.0d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F699D8ACB0E6834"]
			description: ["The iron of the shield casings, recovered from the spent Fe-56 cask of the nickel-56 line. The hot cell, 600 ticks: a spent Fe-56 cask and programmed circuit 26 give a stack of iron-56 in dust form and some lead plate. The dust is pressed to plate as any metal. The Fe-56 shield casing, the primordial cryostat casing, the void diamond window and the horizon gate casing. Casks by ME from the nickel-56 line; the lead returns to the lead stock."]
			icon: "gtceu:iron_56_plate"
			id: "7335D4747766C328"
			rewards: [{ id: "70415B6EE66B9C3C", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "11F12EDA9BB184A0", item: "gtceu:iron_56_plate", type: "item" }]
			title: "Iron-56"
			x: 23.5d
			y: 16.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F699D8ACB0E6834"]
			description: ["The ribbon of the tether: sixteen Kerr strand wires laid on a ribbon segment. It carries the load that the proof test then confirms. The tether ribbon works, 800 ticks: 16 Kerr strand wires, a tether ribbon segment and programmed circuit 14. The proof test then loads two ribbons with liquid helium, which is returned as gas. The proof-loaded ribbon of the star-lift tether. Wire by ME; the helium goes through a cooler back to liquid."]
			icon: "grindless:kerr_ribbon"
			id: "1D3FAA1486FCF60D"
			rewards: [{ id: "360DD9882C943AD5", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "39877165E0062B10", item: "grindless:kerr_ribbon", type: "item" }]
			title: "Kerr Ribbon"
			x: 23.5d
			y: 18.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D3FAA1486FCF60D"]
			description: ["The clock of the launch line: two nuclear clocks and thorium plate tuned together, so that a probe knows where it is by the beat of a nucleus. The nuclear clock lab, 1,200 ticks: two nuclear clocks, eight thorium plate, programmed circuit 9 and argon. The navigation core of the probe. Clocks from their own line by ME; argon by pipe."]
			icon: "grindless:thorium_nav_clock"
			id: "55854E480E3A83F7"
			rewards: [{ id: "5F208686878293E3", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "7D34AC404C2E00E9", item: "grindless:thorium_nav_clock", type: "item" }]
			title: "Thorium Navigation Clock"
			x: 26.0d
			y: 18.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1EBBE33BC966BE23"]
			description: ["The machines of the era, in the order you meet them, each with the first products it makes."]
			icon: "gtceu:hyperfactory"
			id: "742CA0A14D1BC9CC"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "5334342554B57EB9", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Machines of MAX+"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1EBBE33BC966BE23"]
			description: ["The only machine that handles &6Kerr Condensate&r. It settles the fluid and binds older exotic matter into it: strange matter, neutronium, degenerate billets, strand cladding and the cells the components use. It runs anywhere. The MAX hull, a shell of condensate vessel casing round a superfluid core, and condensate from the mirror shell. Every bound material, and the strand that makes the MAX+ cable. Its boil-off goes back into the first recipe, and spent cells go to the helium plant, so nothing is vented."]
			icon: "gtceu:condensate_refinery"
			id: "3DC03C5D536BC546"
			rewards: [{ id: "1FC00FB7B9A86E54", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "52F9C989A8C7426E", item: "gtceu:condensate_refinery", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7FD3206E71E471AA", item: "grindless:condensate_vessel_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Condensate Refinery"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3DC03C5D536BC546"]
			description: ["Its fourth recipe clads a strand of strange matter in condensate. It is the start of the cable line, which the Circuits section finishes at the wire."]
			icon: "grindless:kerr_clad_strand"
			id: "5A7BA6549A3327C6"
			rewards: [{ id: "325FDB2FADA0EF1A", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "12A4D9A57DF8139F", item: "grindless:kerr_clad_strand", type: "item" }]
			title: "Strand Cladding"
			x: 13.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3DC03C5D536BC546"]
			description: ["Condensate will not travel loose, so the helium plant jackets it in a cell. This is the form in which it leaves the shell."]
			icon: "grindless:jacketed_condensate_cell"
			id: "394F32923B8B8A39"
			rewards: [{ id: "341141E62846A28F", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "10E5A59E4A9ABD98", item: "grindless:jacketed_condensate_cell", type: "item" }]
			title: "Jacketed Condensate Cell"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3DC03C5D536BC546"]
			description: ["Neutronium pellets, pressed at a megabar, are bound into the fluid here. The press then turns the ingot into the plate that half the era is built from."]
			icon: "grindless:bound_neutronium_ingot"
			id: "1070580FADAC9107"
			rewards: [{ id: "75B1426237B11846", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "55E5A3795192F0AD", item: "grindless:bound_neutronium_ingot", type: "item" }]
			title: "Bound Neutronium Ingot"
			x: 10.5d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1E02DD0C6E528775"]
			description: ["The &6Bound-Matter Press&r makes the compressed plate, and a laminate, in numbers no other machine can reach. It runs anywhere. The MAX hull, a block of bound press casing, and bound ingots from the refinery. Parts and wear are explained in the casing's tooltip. Horizon compressed plate by the ten thousand, and graded laminate for shielding. Feed ingots by ME and send the plates onward on a belt; the press flash goes back to its own input."]
			icon: "gtceu:bound_matter_press"
			id: "19E22CAE70354C74"
			rewards: [{ id: "3040B25014CABD08", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7DFCCBDE769E2E2F", item: "gtceu:bound_matter_press", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1EC31D7E9E0EC743", item: "grindless:bound_press_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Bound-Matter Press"
			x: 5.5d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19E22CAE70354C74"]
			description: ["A ceramic cermet pressed in layers, the second use of the press. It is the first piece of the shielding that the loom weaves later."]
			icon: "grindless:graded_horizon_laminate"
			id: "3F3FF58351EDB8DB"
			rewards: [{ id: "341A30F3C1D2394F", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5D5D7CAA3F98EEBB", item: "grindless:graded_horizon_laminate", type: "item" }]
			title: "Graded Laminate"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3C5683E2C308B18E"]
			description: ["Out of the Galaxy without a rocket. It binds a probe to a counterweight, then drops the pair on a plunging orbit past the hole. The tide splits them, and the probe leaves at speed. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, and a capture ring of slingshot coil casing wound round counterweight cores. It works only at Sgr A* orbit. The launched probe, and with it every gate that leaves the Galaxy. One counterweight per launch. The weight falls into the hole, so make them in bulk."]
			icon: "gtceu:hills_slingshot"
			id: "5C6CD9758C5ECD8E"
			rewards: [{ id: "35123FE49B98DB77", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3E895C36C995CAC4", item: "gtceu:hills_slingshot", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1F19AD4CF6FAFAA2", item: "grindless:slingshot_coil_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Hills Slingshot"
			x: 10.5d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["384B7591D0DEE491"]
			description: ["Magnetic fields heat a star's outer layers and funnel them off. At the very massive stars of R136 the lift reaches core plasma that no smaller star shows. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, lift nozzles and a tower of lift nozzle casing. It lifts only at the Tarantula. The raw plasma that the filter and former refine for the crucible. Its nozzle wears one in thirty-two runs. Keep a pattern for spare nozzles."]
			icon: "gtceu:tarantula_stellar_lift"
			id: "15F0160069BFFC67"
			rewards: [{ id: "346E27C15B8FEDF9", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3662D2573F79E368", item: "gtceu:tarantula_stellar_lift", type: "item" }
				{ id: "119DB64B0C91A051", item: "grindless:lift_nozzle_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Tarantula Stellar Lift"
			x: 18.5d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["357A817798DE0B18"]
			description: ["The nozzle sits in the hottest part of the lift and wears out. The lift's controller and its casing are built with nozzles too, so make them first; a spare in the bus is a lift that never stops."]
			icon: "grindless:vms_lift_nozzle"
			id: "384B7591D0DEE491"
			rewards: [{ id: "79817ACB64D48C9D", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "129699563ED05A17", item: "grindless:vms_lift_nozzle", type: "item" }]
			title: "Lift Nozzle"
			x: 17.0d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["31F7B42913E1EC19"]
			description: ["Stars above about 140 solar masses end by making nickel-56 in bulk. The crucible forces that burn on lifted plasma in a magnetic pinch. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, liners and a sphere of crucible liner casing; then confined plasma to burn. Nickel-56 slugs, the fuel of the burner, and a silicon-rich ash. The ash is not waste: it goes to a separation row, which can run anywhere. The liner wears one in sixteen runs."]
			icon: "gtceu:pair_instability_crucible"
			id: "54CF2F2C523D9619"
			rewards: [{ id: "706C993277C401A7", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "52C97EECC715E131", item: "gtceu:pair_instability_crucible", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7DDEA395B8478741", item: "grindless:crucible_liner_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Pair-Instability Crucible"
			x: 22.0d
			y: -4.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54CF2F2C523D9619"]
			description: ["Silicon, sulfur, calcium and argon come out of the pinch with the nickel. A separation row takes them back, so the crucible makes no waste."]
			icon: "grindless:ime_ash"
			id: "7714777E1C8EF7F2"
			rewards: [{ id: "15F1D3DD8FEE47D5", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "7E86D63D234C73E0", item: "grindless:ime_ash", type: "item" }]
			title: "Intermediate-Mass Ash"
			x: 23.5d
			y: -6.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["161B334AA960BA09"]
			description: ["The liner takes the whole pinch. The crucible's controller and casing are built with liners too, and they wear quickly, so a spare belongs in every chest the crucible draws from."]
			icon: "grindless:crucible_liner"
			id: "31F7B42913E1EC19"
			rewards: [{ id: "381E4725434E9C25", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5AD5913009305E46", item: "grindless:crucible_liner", type: "item" }]
			title: "Crucible Liner"
			x: 20.5d
			y: -4.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3232ED493BE40B9D"]
			description: ["A supernova glows on the decay of nickel-56 into cobalt, then iron. The burner turns that heat into power through supercritical carbon dioxide, in two recipes. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, a supercritical CO2 turbine module, and shielded casks of nickel-56 from the crucible. A generator of the era. How it feeds the network is in the Integration section. A cask is used twice and comes out as iron. Loop it to the hot cell."]
			icon: "gtceu:nickel_56_burner"
			id: "599D0970AE701F01"
			rewards: [{ id: "3799A00AD1ABBE64", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "7FCAF09F54D695F0", item: "gtceu:nickel_56_burner", type: "item" }]
			title: "Nickel-56 Burner"
			x: 26.5d
			y: -4.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5904BFC41192005D"]
			description: ["After two decays the cask holds iron-56. The hot cell takes it apart and gives the iron back."]
			icon: "grindless:spent_fe56_cask"
			id: "326768002226073D"
			rewards: [{ id: "3506A32E5ED9D7BD", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "31A8E2CC7B49ECA7", item: "grindless:spent_fe56_cask", type: "item" }]
			title: "Spent Iron Cask"
			x: 29.5d
			y: -6.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["39E7AED162176BD5"]
			description: ["The Stream's gas has a tenth of solar metals, with deuterium close to the Big Bang value. A magnetic scoop gathers it as the &6Pristine Gas&r the works refines. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, and magnetic scoop modules. It sweeps only in the Stream. Primordial deuterium and pristine helium-3, the fuel of the torus. The hydrogen the tower strips out goes back to your hydrogen lines by AE2."]
			icon: "gtceu:pristine_gas_works"
			id: "16EBA71D0DE35B6E"
			rewards: [{ id: "15C6733CC6A46866", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "302847534A5B0929", item: "gtceu:pristine_gas_works", type: "item" }]
			title: "Pristine Gas Works"
			x: 24.25d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1A7ECED9F7530435"]
			description: ["A cold coil on a long arm. It gathers the gas: the works is built with one, and every sweep wears a little of it."]
			icon: "grindless:magnetic_scoop_module"
			id: "39E7AED162176BD5"
			rewards: [{ id: "7B2CADD7D1A5515A", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "367D522937A3F60B", item: "grindless:magnetic_scoop_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Magnetic Scoop Module"
			x: 22.75d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3A94112D7B78FC78", "3BD80291F79AD42F"]
			description: ["Deuterium and helium-3 fuse with few neutrons, and a direct converter catches their charged products. It is a generator of ours, not a GTM fusion tier. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, a beam injector and a converter stack; then deuterium and helium-3 together. A second generator of the era. How it feeds the network is in the Integration section. It burns only in the Stream. Pipe both fuels in from their lines."]
			icon: "gtceu:primordial_fusion_torus"
			id: "5DE3FE0F732840CC"
			rewards: [{ id: "14EBF160CDACDD63", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "3E9EFFCD73123160", item: "gtceu:primordial_fusion_torus", type: "item" }]
			title: "Primordial Fusion Torus"
			x: 28.75d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DFE1272DB6130B6"]
			description: ["A beam of neutral deuterium heats the fuel to ignition. The torus is built with one, and it wears one in sixty-four runs."]
			icon: "grindless:neutral_beam_injector"
			id: "3A94112D7B78FC78"
			rewards: [{ id: "5BE12A186919C4B0", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3315AC8C409705AD", item: "grindless:neutral_beam_injector", type: "item" }]
			title: "Neutral Beam Injector"
			x: 27.25d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["164DF010E9BE6259"]
			description: ["The stack turns the charged products of deuterium and helium-3 straight into current. The torus is built with one, and it wears one in a hundred and twenty-eight runs."]
			icon: "grindless:direct_converter_stack"
			id: "3BD80291F79AD42F"
			rewards: [{ id: "522F251BE9625CC0", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "16FA749F10C1E7DD", item: "grindless:direct_converter_stack", type: "item" }]
			title: "Direct Converter Stack"
			x: 27.25d
			y: -3.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DE3FE0F732840CC"]
			description: ["Deuterium and helium-3 with aligned spins fuse with about one and a half times the torus's energy per fuel. This generator of ours runs up to sixty-four runs at once. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, and a whole primordial fusion torus, which the controller consumes, plus turbine modules, converter stacks and beam injectors; then P26 fuel. One plant for a consumer of 2^39 EU/t: eight 64 A wireless dynamo hatches give 2^40 EU/t. How it feeds the network is in the Integration section. Send pellets and polarized helium-3 from home by AE2; the plant runs anywhere. More dynamo hatches give more runs, up to eight for sixty-four. Keep spares of the three worn parts."]
			icon: "gtceu:polarized_fusion_stellarator"
			id: "1DEF144DD280F570"
			rewards: [{ id: "777DA36D0E1B6BA5", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "5A98B0113145F086", item: "gtceu:polarized_fusion_stellarator", type: "item" }]
			title: "Polarized Fusion Stellarator"
			x: 30.25d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1DEF144DD280F570"]
			description: ["Pure HD is polarized by brute force at millikelvin in the cryostat works, then extruded into pellets. Four pellets and a bucket of polarized helium-3, which the photonic foundry pumps by laser from line P10's helium-3, make one run."]
			icon: "grindless:polarized_hd_pellet"
			id: "7989D356A54F2605"
			rewards: [{ id: "18900B8FDB76E554", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3F21469F53B1D674", item: "grindless:polarized_hd_pellet", type: "item" }]
			title: "Polarized HD Pellet"
			x: 31.75d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5851F26D0448CBBB"]
			description: ["Light falling to a factory held near a horizon arrives blueshifted, as gamma rays. The forge uses that bath for photonuclear reactions that make the rare isotopes. The MAX hull with horizon casings, MAX+ circuits and components, and compressed plates; then a deep tether and molybdenum targets to run it. It works only at the M31 nucleus. Photonuclear isotopes, which no other machine can make. The tether and window wear one in thirty-two runs; keep spares."]
			icon: "gtceu:blueshift_forge"
			id: "7D19550CD975EC8E"
			rewards: [{ id: "772096B08BD7544C", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "7D7807BE134E2993", item: "gtceu:blueshift_forge", type: "item" }]
